# Mariachi Framework (consumer)

The framework docs ship in `node_modules/@mariachi/core/docs/`. Start at `README.md` there, then read:

- `node_modules/@mariachi/core/docs/architecture.md`: layers, project layout, import boundaries
- `node_modules/@mariachi/core/docs/conventions.md`: rules enforced by `mariachi validate`
- `node_modules/@mariachi/core/docs/patterns.md`: composition root, DI, context, errors, idempotency
- `node_modules/@mariachi/core/docs/packages.md`: every package, with status and entry points
- `node_modules/@mariachi/core/docs/ai-guide.md`: which piece to use, and common mistakes
- `node_modules/@mariachi/core/docs/recipes/`: entity, job, webhook, integration, wiring

## Critical rules

- `ctx` first, always: `communication.call(ctx, 'domain.action', input)`, handlers `(ctx, input)`, jobs `(ctx, data)`
- Controllers never import services or database packages; shared schemas live in `src/contracts/`
- Throw `MariachiError` subclasses with a `code`, never raw `Error`
- No `process.env` outside config
- Relative imports are extensionless
- Zod at boundaries (routes, procedures, jobs, events, config)
- Generate code with `mariachi generate <entity|service|controller|job|integration> <name>` and check with `mariachi validate`

To use this rule in Cursor, copy it to your project's `.cursor/rules/`. Projects created by `mariachi init` get an `AGENTS.md` with the same pointers.
